  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Let $P(x)=(x-p)(x-q)(x-r)$ where $p,q,r>0$. Show that the coefficients of $P(x)$ alternate in their signs.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=x^3-(p+q+r)x^2+(pq+pr+qr)x-pqr$.\n\nSince $p,q,r>0$, the coefficient signs are $+,-,+,-$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=[x^2-(p+q)x+pq](x-r)\\\\P(x)&=x^3-(p+q+r)x^2+(pq+pr+qr)x-pqr\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $p,q,r>0$, the quantities $p+q+r$, $pq+pr+qr$ and $pqr$ are positive. In descending powers, the coefficient signs are therefore $+,-,+,-$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
